course: dictionary
lesson: 2794
title: Displace: pushed out of place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Displace» means to push something out of its place, or to take its place. Read the words around it to find the meaning. Then test your idea by putting it in the sentence in place of the hard word.
explain: «The floods displaced hundreds of families from their homes.» The families had to leave their homes, so displace can mean to force people out of where they live. Floods and wars are common reasons.
explain: «A floating object pushes aside, or displaces, some water.» Here the clue is pushes aside. The word means to push something out of the way, so when a boat floats, it pushes water out of its way.
fact: Displace has three main meanings: to push out of place, to force people to leave their homes, and in science to push aside water or another liquid.
fact: «Displaced people» are people forced to leave their homes, often by war or floods.
fact: An «internally displaced person» has been forced from home but is still inside their own country.
fact: When an object goes into water, it displaces water: the water it pushes aside has the same volume as the part of the object under the water.
fact: Measuring displaced water is a way to find the volume of an object with an odd shape.
exercise: «The floods displaced hundreds of families from their homes.» What does displaced mean here? | Cleaned and tidied | *Forced to leave their homes | Painted bright colours | Given a brand new house for free
exercise: «A floating object pushes aside, or displaces, some water.» In this sentence, what is displaced? | The object's colour | The bath | *The water | The sky
exercise: Which phrase means people who are forced from home but are still in their own country? | Happy holidaymakers | Water engineers | *Internally displaced persons | Football fans
test: «Displaced people» are people who have been what? | Lost in a shop | Asleep in a tent for a week | *Forced from their homes | Given a prize for running
test: When you drop a marble into a full jug of water, what is displaced? | The table underneath | *The water, which spills over the top | The marble's name | The jug's handle
exam: In science, what does an object do to water when it is put into it? | It turns the water into ice | *It pushes some of the water aside | It makes the water sing | It changes the water's colour
